      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WOODSTOCK ROCK (5) gets the nod after an excellent Emerald win two back, then a sound Mackay second behind Contemporary over 1050m. The return to 1200m suits on his record, and his overall strike rate and wet-track consistency make him the most reliable option, although he was beaten as a well-backed runner last time. HUMBLE HERO (4) brings the strongest winning habit, having won a Benchmark 68 at Mackay after scoring in Benchmark 58 grade at Rockhampton, and his record with Natalea Summers is a major tick. ELLIBABY (10) was below market expectation at Thangool, but her narrow Emerald second two back and proven 1200m form keep her right in the race. ASTAPOR (8) is the value place threat: he has placed in both runs this prep, gets weight relief from Moree, and has already been competitive at Emerald, but needs to turn the tables on WOODSTOCK ROCK to win.",
